1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,761
How much does an electric car add to your home's electric bill?

2
00:00:03,881 --> 00:00:04,786
Here's the math.

3
00:00:04,906 --> 00:00:10,076
The average car in America drives about eleven thousand twenty-six miles a year.

4
00:00:10,196 --> 00:00:16,278
At thirty kilowatt-hours per hundred miles, that's about three thousand three hundred eight kilowatt-hours.

5
00:00:16,398 --> 00:00:22,615
The average American home uses about ten thousand seven hundred ninety-one kilowatt-hours a year.

6
00:00:22,735 --> 00:00:24,919
So the car adds about thirty-one percent.

7
00:00:25,039 --> 00:00:28,597
Per month, that's about two hundred seventy-six kilowatt-hours.

8
00:00:28,717 --> 00:00:31,206
At the national price, about fifty dollars.

9
00:00:31,326 --> 00:00:35,736
Gas for the same miles would cost about one hundred five dollars a month.

10
00:00:35,856 --> 00:00:37,856
So yes, your power bill goes up.

11
00:00:37,976 --> 00:00:39,608
But your gas bill goes away.

12
00:00:39,728 --> 00:00:43,819
So, how much does an electric car add to your home's electric bill?

13
00:00:43,939 --> 00:00:45,569
About fifty dollars a month.
